diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b394bb9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+## Deployment
+
+Fizzy includes a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org/) configuration for running the complete application on one Linux server. The application uses SQLite, stores uploads on local disk, and runs Solid Queue alongside Puma in the web container. Kamal Proxy handles HTTPS with an automatically renewed Let's Encrypt certificate.
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+The server must be reachable over SSH and have Docker installed. Ports 80 and 443 must be open. Point the DNS record for your Fizzy hostname at the server before deploying so Let's Encrypt can issue its certificate. You also need Docker on the computer from which you deploy.
+
+### Configure the deployment
+
+Edit the values at the top of [`config/deploy.yml`](../config/deploy.yml):
+
+- Replace `fizzy.example.com` with the hostname of the server.
+- Replace `smtp.example.com` with the address of your SMTP server.
+- Set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` to the address Fizzy should send from.
+- Adjust the SMTP port, domain, authentication method, or STARTTLS setting if required by your mail provider.
+- Change `builder.arch` if the server is not AMD64.
+- Increase `WEB_CONCURRENCY` or `JOB_CONCURRENCY` if the server has enough memory and needs more throughput.
+
+Kamal connects as `root` by default. Add an `ssh.user` setting to `config/deploy.yml` if Docker is available through another SSH user.
+
+Set the secrets referenced by [`.kamal/secrets`](../.kamal/secrets) in your shell:
+
+```sh
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE="$(bin/rails secret)"
+export SMTP_USERNAME="your-smtp-user"
+export SMTP_PASSWORD="your-smtp-password"
+```
+
+Store `SECRET_KEY_BASE` in a password manager and reuse the same value for every deployment. Changing it invalidates existing sessions and signed links. You can replace the environment references in `.kamal/secrets` with commands for your secret manager if preferred; do not commit raw secret values.
+
+### Deploy
+
+Set up the server and deploy Fizzy:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Fizzy will be available at `https://your-hostname`. Later releases can be deployed with:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+The `fizzy_storage` Docker volume contains all SQLite databases and uploaded files and is mounted into each new application container, so data survives deployments. Back up this volume as part of the server's normal backup plan; removing the volume deletes the application data.
